<speak>All right. I have finished writing the practical reminders for myself. There are only a few: separate the personal tray, stop taking the loose papers home in the business bag, and look at the diary before arranging another appointment. That is manageable. If I made a much longer list, I would probably put it under the same pile we have been talking about and never see it again. My wife will laugh when I tell her the bank conversation included my filing habits, but she will be pleased if I actually do something about them instead of merely describing the problem very eloquently.</speak>